{
  "manifest_version": "1.0.0",
  "spec": "CODE-JUNCTION/BRIDGECAD_GAD_ACCEPTANCE_RESOLUTION.md §4",
  "note": [
    "Required content per drawing area, as a versioned reviewable manifest. Each entry names a stable ID, the drawing area, the target sheet, the measurable evidence and the declared implementation status; a reviewer verdict field is present but blank until a human signs a row off.",
    "A requirement is only credited when it is declared IMPLEMENTED here AND measured present in the generated DXF. A PARTIAL or MISSING declaration is reported as a gap so the REQUIRED_CONTENT gate cannot pass on a declared-but-unbuilt feature.",
    "Measurement is deliberately weak evidence: it proves a declared layer/label/schedule is on the sheet, not that a detail is correct. Correct physical levels and connectivity are proven separately by the GEOMETRY_CONTRACT gate; title-block presence and zone collisions by the LAYOUT gate; and structural adequacy by the ENGINEERING_REVIEW gate.",
    "`when` conditions scope a requirement to the resolved parameters (e.g. a pile schedule only applies to a pile-foundation card). A requirement whose condition does not match is reported applicable=false and excluded from the pass set rather than silently passing.",
    "`abutment_shape_family` is derived from the same bridgecad_core.geometry.abutment_profiles.family_for() the renderers use, so the cantilever and battered area checks track the drawn shape family rather than a hand-kept list.",
    "`scope` keeps drawing text and title-block text apart: drawing-content requirements default to scope=drawing and cannot be satisfied by title-block boilerplate (a project name such as 'PROJECT: Open Foundation ...' must not stand in for an open-footing label). Only the RC-TTL-* title/notes requirements set scope=title_block.",
    "Supersedes the scaffold-level tests/draw/sheets.spec.json for acceptance purposes: that file still names layer prefixes (CL/DIM/GRID/HTCH/TABL) the renderers no longer emit."
  ],
